  "local_adaptations": [
    "Rename the skill to pr-babysit and keep only one target pull request.",
    "Keep snapshot-first ordering, current-head invalidation, and exact branch-currency evidence.",
    "Replace host skill calls and user questions with native-session handoff language.",
    "Use only the caller-supplied state directory and one checkpoint per turn.",
    "Add native bounded repair dispatch, least-privilege credential fencing, and safe SHA/thread result handling.",
    "Treat every branch-currency item as a human decision, never an automatic claim.",
    "Adapt report status examples from Unicode symbols and em dashes to ASCII text and hyphen punctuation while retaining the upstream source hash.",
    "Retain only the deployed snapshot command and canonical identity flags while preserving all normalization helpers.",
    "Return the observed head from snapshots and reconcile it through the durable checkpoint fence instead of rejecting head drift.",
    "Add bounded local feedback disposition by stable item identity and reopen changed content.",
    "Carry confirmed review IDs until the next snapshot marks their current identities.",
    "Key repair attempt budgets by action kind, fingerprint, and observed head SHA.",
    "Bind repair validation to a persisted candidate head and independent reviewer verdict.",
    "Require structured current-snapshot merge-ready evidence and use crash-safe same-directory state writes.",
    "Expose the deterministic state CLI through the city-scoped core-city pack and keep the rig-imported pack command-free."
  ]
